course: dictionary
lesson: 7200
title: Old words with tricky meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Pettifog is a very old and rare word, so you may not know it at all. When you meet it, read the words around it. In «Toad blames the pettifogging mistrustfulness of paid officials», Toad is blaming someone else, and the word pettifogging describes the officials as fussy.
explain: Ask yourself what would fit. Try the meaning "fussy about small things" in the sentence: «Toad blames the fussy mistrustfulness of paid officials.» It still makes sense, so that is a good meaning.
explain: The sentence ends with "really it is his own fault", which is a clue that Toad is wrong to blame the officials. Their fussiness about small details is not the real cause of the trouble.
fact: To pettifog means to argue about small, unimportant details in a fussy way.
fact: Pettifogging means fussy about tiny things. A pettifogger is a petty, tricky lawyer who works on small, mean cases.
fact: Pettifog is old and rare, so you will mostly find it in old books.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word. A good check is to swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «Toad blames the pettifogging mistrustfulness of paid officials.» What does pettifogging mean here? | Loud and cheerful | Sleepy after a long meal | Kind and generous with money | *Fussy about small things
exercise: What is a pettifogger? | *A petty, tricky lawyer who works on small, mean cases | A judge who is never wrong | A baker who makes small cakes | A tiny fish found in rivers
exercise: Find and copy the word from «Toad blames the pettifogging mistrustfulness of paid officials» that describes the officials' fussy behaviour. | officials | *pettifogging | Toad | paid
test: What does it mean to pettifog? | To run very fast in a race | To cook a big meal for friends | *To argue fussily about small, unimportant details
test: Why might you rarely meet the word pettifog in modern books? | It is a word for a kind of cake | It only means something in a petrol station | *It is old and rare, so it is found mostly in old books | It is a brand new slang word that only teenagers use
exam: Ella finds pettifogging in an old book and does not know it. What should she do first? | Skip the whole book and never read it | *Read the words around it and try a meaning in the sentence | Guess a random word without checking the sentence | Ask the nearest petrol station
